n" [:option {:value "158414"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158425"} "Coxed Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158447"} "Coxed Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "158458"} "Eights, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "157531"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "9017151"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "157556"} "1908"] "\n" [:option {:value "157696"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "157811"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "157904"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "157967"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "158055"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "158181"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "158275"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "158357"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "158519"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "158610"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "158701"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "158831"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "158952"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "159078"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "159249"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "159415"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "159600"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159776"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261021"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319191"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353991"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19008468"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2012468"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/385"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Coxless Fours, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 – 15 October 1964"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/469"} "Toda Rowing Course, Toda, Saitama"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158436"} "57 from 14 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The United States was the reigning Olympic and Pan American champion in the coxless fours. In addition to veteran Olympian " [:a {:href "/athletes/40815"} "Ted Nash"] ", they also sent " [:a {:href "/athletes/40833"} "Geoffrey Picard"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/40762"} "Dick Lyon"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/40797"} "Ted Mittet"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40630"} "Philip Durbrow"] ". Germany, meanwhile, had won the last two European Championships and the inaugural World Championships, and sent their reigning European champions, " [:a {:href "/athletes/37990"} "Günter Schrörs"] ", 1960 Olympic champion in the coxed fours " [:a {:href "/athletes/37789"} "Horst Effertz"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/37931"} "Albrecht Müller"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37928"} "Manfred Misselhorn"] " to Tokyo. England had been the victors at the most recent British Empire and Commonwealth Games and, although Great Britain sent a different squad to the 1964 Summer Games, they were considered a medal contender in the coxless fours."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Germany had the most impressive run in the opening round, while Great Britain and Denmark won the other heats. Denmark was represented by the most recent European silver medalists: " [:a {:href "/athletes/36500"} "John Ørsted Hansen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/36584"} "Erik Petersen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/36509"} "Kurt Helmudt"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36507"} "Bjørn Borgen Hasløv"] ". The Americans advanced to the finals through the repêchage, but did not look strong compared to the other heat winners, Italy and the Netherlands. Three of Italy’s rowers, " [:a {:href "/athletes/38490"} "Romano Sgheiz"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/38277"} "Fulvio Balatti"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38536"} "Giovanni Zucchi"] ", were bronze medalists from the 1960 Olympic coxed fours event (and Sgheiz was a champion from the same event in 1956) and, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/38489"} "Luciano Sgheiz"] ", had won silver and bronze at the 1963 and 1964 European Championships respectively. The race for podium spots was close and exciting: just over two seconds separated the surprise gold medalists, Denmark, from the bronze medal-winning Americans, with the Britons sandwiched in-between with silver. This was the former rowing power of Great Britain’s first Olympic medal since 1948, as well as Denmark’s first gold medal since then."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Denmark"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/36500"} "John Ørsted Hansen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36584"} "Erik Petersen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36509"} "Kurt Helmudt"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36507"} "Bjørn Borgen Hasløv"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/37454"} "John M. Russell"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37500"} "Hugh Wardell-Yerburgh"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37208"} "Bill Barry"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37339"} "John James"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align